[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:One Man in a Boat]
[00:15.15]Why is fishing the writer's favourite sport?
[00:22.27]Fishing is my favourite sport.
[00:26.20]I often fish for hours without catching anything.
[00:31.64]But this does not worry me.
[00:35.02]Some fishermen are unlucky.
[00:38.16]Instead of catching fish,
[00:40.55]they catch old boots and rubbish.
[00:44.35]I am even less lucky.
[00:47.04]I never catch anything --not even old boots.
[00:52.39]After having spent whole mornings on the river,
[00:56.56]I always go home with an empty bag.
[01:00.94]'You must give up fishing!'
[01:03.50]my friends say. 'It's a waste of time.'
[01:09.10]But they don't realize one important thing.
[01:14.22]I'm not really interested in fishing.
[01:17.87]I am only interested in sitting in a boat and doing nothing at all!
